 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "System software runs the computer itself; application software does tasks for the user (word processor, browser, games).\nThe operating system (OS) is the most important system software. It starts when the computer is switched on and manages everything:\n• memory (RAM) and the processor (running programs);\n• files and folders;\n• devices (printer, keyboard, screen);\n• security (user accounts, passwords);\n• the user interface.\nInterfaces: a graphical user interface (GUI) with windows, icons, menus and a pointer; a command-line interface (CLI) where commands are typed.\nExamples: Windows, macOS and Linux (computers); Android and iOS (phones and tablets).",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "o": "Android"
  },
  "problem": "Is {o} system software or application software? Explain.",
  "steps": [
   "{o} is an operating system: it manages the phone's memory, files, devices and screen.",
   "Apps such as WhatsApp run on top of it."
  ],
  "answer": "System software (an operating system).",
  "checks": []
 },
